p='body2.md'; s=open(p).read()
R=[
("Circuit Oracle (Kabir et al. 2026) is the closest task: an LLM harness reads transcoder attribution graphs of Gemma-2-2B probes and judges whether a spurious cue *named in its prompt* dominates, scored by an LLM judge (78.2%, vs 77.5% for a one-shot readout). Its framework has intervention tools, but its spurious-cue task neither requires nor scores causal verification or removal. ShiftHunt withholds the cue and the number of cues, rations exact queries, and checks an executable detector and its removal in closed form on held-out notes: it asks whether the claim holds on independent data, not whether the report sounds right, and §4.3 shows that the two can come apart completely. Pando (Zhong et al. 2026) grades exactly against a budget-matched black-box arm, for a fixed pipeline on 10 random queries, and calls adaptive querying \"a natural next step\"; ShiftHunt evaluates that setting, and C1 refines Pando's finding that SAE methods add little over sample-only: under a scarce, adaptively spent budget the SAE ranking is worth 16-64 exact queries. Karvonen et al. (2024) automate SHIFT with an oracle-normalized score, and Nusrat and Nusrat (2026) grade naming and repair exactly on small clinical networks.",
 "Circuit Oracle (Kabir et al. 2026) is the closest task: an LLM harness reads attribution graphs of Gemma-2-2B probes and judges whether a spurious cue *named in its prompt* dominates, scored by an LLM judge (78.2%, vs 77.5% for a one-shot readout); its spurious-cue task neither requires nor scores causal verification or removal. ShiftHunt withholds the cue and the number of cues, rations exact queries, and checks an executable detector and its removal in closed form on held-out notes, i.e. whether the claim holds on independent data rather than whether the report sounds right; §4.3 shows the two can come apart completely. Pando (Zhong et al. 2026) grades exactly against a budget-matched black-box arm for a fixed pipeline on 10 random queries and calls adaptive querying \"a natural next step\"; we evaluate that setting, and C1 refines its finding that SAE methods add little over sample-only: under a scarce, adaptively spent budget the SAE ranking is worth 16-64 exact queries. Karvonen et al. (2024) automate SHIFT with an oracle-normalized score; Nusrat and Nusrat (2026) grade naming and repair exactly on small clinical networks."),
("Gogleva et al. (2026) instead locate failure at evidence use; GX-Chen et al. (2025) find conjunctive causes under-hypothesized. Informative priors suppress exploration in LLM bandits (Austin et al. 2026; Krishnamurthy et al. 2024); guided attribution patching (Zhang et al. 2026) is human-designed widening across a proxy's ranking. Prediction-powered inference and active testing (Angelopoulos et al. 2023; Ashouritaklimi et al. 2026) use proxies for *estimation*; we measure *acquisition*, and PROBE (Ma et al. 2026) shows why trusting an uncalibrated proxy is anti-conservative. AstaBench reports judge-expert agreement at system level; J1-J4 measure it on single decisive slots against executed ground truth, and Table 5 shows the consequence for rankings. ABC (Zhu et al. 2025) documents a judge accepting empty replies, an analogue of our \"nothing found\" false credit; we follow it, BenchJack (Wang et al. 2026) and ImpossibleBench (Zhong et al. 2025) on validity and exploits.",
 "Informative priors suppress exploration in LLM bandits (Austin et al. 2026; Krishnamurthy et al. 2024); guided attribution patching (Zhang et al. 2026) is human-designed widening across a proxy's ranking. Prediction-powered inference and active testing (Angelopoulos et al. 2023; Ashouritaklimi et al. 2026) use proxies for *estimation*; we measure *acquisition* (cf. PROBE: trusting an uncalibrated proxy is anti-conservative; Ma et al. 2026). AstaBench reports judge-expert agreement at system level; J1-J4 measure it on decisive slots against executed ground truth. ABC (Zhu et al. 2025) documents a judge accepting empty replies, an analogue of our \"nothing found\" false credit; we follow it, BenchJack (Wang et al. 2026) and ImpossibleBench (Zhong et al. 2025) on validity and exploits."),
("It *raises* rank-2 testing (21/72 vs 7/72): it concentrates tests on its head, not on rank 1 alone. Across all four agents with the proxy the curve is 76 / 20 / 7 / 0.4%, and on 208 of 231 planted probes the tested set is exactly the proxy's top-k for some k (8.9× the rank-blind rate; Appendix F). The pre-registered held-out test R1 met its thresholds (November held-out runs alone: 72 / 23 / 8 / 0.5%, a post hoc split), but on the same items with some runs read before, so it is directional; a second held-out prediction, R4 (a fixed share of exact texts to non-hard probes), **failed** (Appendix L).",
 "It *raises* rank-2 testing (21/72 vs 7/72): it concentrates tests on its head, not on rank 1 alone. Across all four agents the curve is 76 / 20 / 7 / 0.4%, and on 208 of 231 planted probes the tested set is exactly a top-k prefix (8.9× the rank-blind rate; Appendix F). Held-out test R1 met its pre-registered thresholds (November held-out runs: 72 / 23 / 8 / 0.5%), but on the same items with some runs read before, so it is directional; held-out prediction R4 (a fixed share of exact texts to non-hard probes) **failed** (Appendix L)."),
("The 4 exceptions are two threshold misreads on the borderline trap item and two [main]s named with an untested extra cue. ",
 "The 4 exceptions are two threshold misreads and two untested extra cues. "),
("Lowering B turns that trace contrast into a score contrast: at B = 4 a blanket top-two policy cannot cover four probes (in an exploratory harder variant with traps at 4 texts, GPT passed 3/4 trap runs). Deepening the truth is the second knob: moving the [main] to proxy rank 3-8 in a counterfactual [PRIV] drops Π₂ to 0.00 while the hedge holds at 0.46-0.56 (a rank-3 item needs a newly trained trap with two decoys).",
 "Lowering B turns that contrast into a score contrast: at B = 4 a blanket top-two policy cannot cover four probes (with traps at 4 texts, GPT passed 3/4 exploratory trap runs). Deepening the truth is the second knob: with the [main] moved to proxy rank 3-8 [PRIV], Π₂ drops to 0.00 while the hedge holds at 0.46-0.56 (such an item needs a newly trained two-decoy trap)."),
("Nothing here is specific to SAEs: M1 needs only items whose proxy error is known, by construction or post hoc (a dev-set metric against a held-out split, a docking score against later assays, an LLM reviewer against replication). §4.3 applies M1-M3 to an LLM judge.",
 "Nothing here is SAE-specific: M1 needs only items whose proxy error is known, by construction or post hoc (a dev-set metric vs a held-out split, a docking score vs later assays). §4.3 applies M1-M3 to an LLM judge."),
("Outcome bits cannot rank agents at this n: with 16 runs per agent only a drop of 0.54 is detectable at 80% power, and the observed GPT-Opus gap needs about 84 runs per agent. Fresh generator items, not more runs, buy item-level power.",
 "Outcome bits cannot rank agents at this n (16 runs per agent detect only a drop of 0.54 at 80% power; the GPT-Opus gap needs about 84 runs each), and fresh items, not more runs, buy item-level power."),
]
